      "answer_seconds": 7.032428399659693,
      "answer": {
        "coverage": "complete",
        "insufficient_evidence": false,
        "summary": "Bangaly Kaba recommends the “managing complex change” framework: check for vision, skills, incentives, resources, and an action plan, then use observed team difficulties to identify what is missing and where to intervene.",
        "summary_citation_ids": [
          "S1",
          "S2",
          "S3"
        ],
        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "Assess the five components",
            "content": "Check whether the team has a clear vision, the skills needed, appropriate incentives, the right resources in the right places, and a clear action plan. Kaba says all five are needed for change.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Use symptoms to locate the gap and choose an intervention",
            "content": "Observe what is happening and the challenges you see, then use the framework’s outcomes as diagnostic clues: missing vision can lead to confusion; missing incentives to resistance; missing skills to anxiety; and missing an action plan to false starts. Once you identify the likely gap, work out what is missing and which levers to pull. Kaba notes that action plans are comparatively easier to institute.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S2",
              "S3"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "missing_topics": []
      },
