      "answer": {
        "coverage": "complete",
        "insufficient_evidence": false,
        "summary": "Bangaly Kaba recommends the “managing complex change” framework: check whether a team has vision, skills, incentives, resources, and an action plan; identify what is missing, then choose the levers to address it. The gap can show up as a characteristic difficulty, such as confusion, resistance, or false starts. [S1, S2, S3]",
        "summary_citation_ids": [
          "S1",
          "S2",
          "S3"
        ],
        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "Assess the five components",
            "content": "Check whether the team has a clear vision, the skills needed, appropriate incentives, resources in the right places, and a clear action plan. Kaba says each is needed for change. [S1]",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Use the difficulty to locate the gap, then act",
            "content": "Observe what is happening and identify challenges both anecdotally and from what you see. Missing vision can lead to confusion; missing incentives to resistance; and missing an action plan to false starts. Skills gaps may show up as anxiety, a mapping Kaba affirms in the discussion. Once you identify the likely bucket, determine what is missing and which levers to pull. Kaba adds that action plans are easier to institute than some other components. [S2, S3]",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S2",
              "S3"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "missing_topics": []
      },
